                <pb facs="0219" n="99" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg99"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4 General Committee/34: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Chairman of the American Delegation
                            (Gibson) to the
                            Acting Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-04-21T17:00:00+01:00">April 21, 1932—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received April 21—2 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>139. Considerable interest is attached to the meeting of the General Commission
                    this morning owing to the presence of MacDonald and Bruening.</p>
                <pb facs="0220" n="100" xml:id="pg100"/>
                <p>The former took occasion during a translation to make a personal appeal to
                        Paul-Boncour in an informal
                    conversation urging him to abandon his opposition to the British resolution
                    telling him that the world was weary with the bickerings at Geneva over words
                    and that he thought that it might help restore the confidence that was nearly
                    lost in the proceedings here if the French would join in the support of a
                    resolution for which there seemed to be such general agreement.</p>
                <p>
                    Paul-Boncour felt, however, that he was
                    unable to respond to MacDonald’s
                    reasoning.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
